{
  "verdict": "trojan_detected",
  "suspect_instances": [
    "u_and_hi"
  ],
  "justification": "Instance u_and_hi in inputs/netlist.v is the suspect gate responsible for the permission-check discrepancy. Analysis of the AND-reduction tree shows that the intermediate high-pair term produced by u_and_hi does not correctly combine eq[2] and eq[3], causing grant to deviate from the expected 4-bit equality comparator behavior for several id_in values, including cases where id_in matches id_auth exactly and cases where id_in differs only at bit index 2. All other instances (u_eq0, u_eq1, u_eq2, u_eq3, u_and_lo, u_and_final) retain their correct, brief-specified primitive bindings and connectivity; only the u_and_hi cell-type binding deviates from design intent, consistent with a synthesis/ECO-stage library-cell substitution trojan that is invisible to structural/topological diffing since instance count, net count, and the AND-reduction tree shape are unchanged.",
  "mismatching_inputs": [
